Package: ecoPortfolio
Type: Package
Title: Climate Risk Metrics for Equity Portfolios
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Moses", "Adebayo", , "adebayomoses2021@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Calculates the carbon metrics recommended for portfolio
    disclosure by the Task Force on Climate-related Financial Disclosures
    (TCFD) and the International Sustainability Standards Board (ISSB):
    weighted average carbon intensity (WACI), financed emissions attributed
    by enterprise value including cash as in the Partnership for Carbon
    Accounting Financials (PCAF) standard, and carbon footprint. Also
    reports data coverage, decomposes the WACI gap to a benchmark into
    sector allocation and stock selection effects, and runs carbon price
    stress tests that translate scenario paths into earnings at risk and
    valuation shocks. Metrics work on emissions data you supply; optional
    helpers download asset-level emissions and owners from the open
    Climate TRACE API <https://climatetrace.org> and match owners to
    holdings by normalised company name.
